[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Analysers low-level requirements
UID: FMD-LLR-ANL
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the analyser item, part ANL, written from the code as built: the framework in
`flightmd_core/analysers/` (`__init__.py`, `base.py`, `registry.py`, `helpers.py`, `phases.py`, `vehicle.py`),
the checks `gps.py`, `battery.py`, `motors.py`, `power.py` and `parameters.py`, the data files
`flightmd_core/data/param_safe_ranges.json` and `flightmd_core/data/param_tables/*.json`, and the generator
`scripts/gen_param_tables.py`. Timestamps are log-relative microseconds (written "us" here). Where the code does
less than its parent asks, the statement says what the code does. The design, with the table of every threshold,
is in `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-anl.md`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Base class (flightmd_core/analysers/base.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: BaseAnalyser declaration
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser` is an abstract class with class attributes `name`, `display_name`, `required_topics` (default
`[]`), `optional_topics` (`[]`), `required_any` (`[]`), `required_columns` (`{}`, topic to list of columns),
`formats` (`[]`, meaning any format), `weight` (`0.0`) and `metadata` (`None`), and one abstract method
`analyse(topics, params)` that returns an `AnalyserResult`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: is_applicable
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser.is_applicable(available_topics)` returns `False` when any name in `required_topics` is not in the
set, else `True` when `required_any` is empty or at least one of its names is in the set, else `False`. It does
not look at `formats` or `required_columns`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: missing_inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser.missing_inputs(topics)` returns the first of these that applies, else `None`:
`"Required topics not available: <names>"` when a required topic is missing; `"Needs one of these topics:
<names>"` when `required_any` is set and none is present; `"Not available for <fmt> logs."` when `formats` is
not empty, `metadata.source_format` is set and is not in `formats`; and, only when `topics` is a dict,
`"<topic> has no <columns> column"` for the first present topic in `required_columns` that lacks a listed
column. A topic that is present with zero rows passes.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Skipped result
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser._skip(reason)` returns an `AnalyserResult` with the analyser's `name` and `display_name`, no
findings, `skipped=True` and `skip_reason=reason`. `skip_result(topics)` returns `_skip` with the text of
`missing_inputs(topics)`, or `"Not applicable to this log."` when that is `None`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: safe_analyse checks inputs first
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser.safe_analyse(topics, params)` calls `missing_inputs(topics)` and, when it returns a reason, returns
`_skip(reason)` without calling `analyse`; otherwise it returns the result of `analyse(topics, params)`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: safe_analyse turns an exception into a skip and times the run
STATEMENT: >>>
`BaseAnalyser.safe_analyse` catches any `Exception` raised by `analyse` and returns
`_skip("Analysis error: <type name>: <message>")`. On every path it sets `result.processing_ms` to the elapsed
wall-clock time in whole milliseconds.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in the analyser test files makes `analyse` raise or reads `processing_ms`. Review checks the
`try`/`except Exception` and the assignment after it.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Registry (flightmd_core/analysers/registry.py, __init__.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Built-in list and order
STATEMENT: >>>
`registry.BUILTINS` lists, in this order, `OscillationAnalyser`, `VibrationAnalyser`, `EKFAnalyser`,
`BatteryAnalyser`, `GPSAnalyser`, `ParameterAnalyser`, `MotorAnalyser`, `AscentProfileAnalyser`, `PowerAnalyser`.
`analyser_classes()` returns `BUILTINS` followed by `plugin_classes()`. The package `flightmd_core.analysers`
re-exports the nine classes and `load_analysers`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: plugin_classes loads and filters entry points
STATEMENT: >>>
`plugin_classes()` reads the entry points of group `flightmd.analysers` (`ENTRY_POINT_GROUP`) and for each one:
logs a warning and leaves it out when `load()` raises any `Exception`, when the loaded object is not a class
derived from `BaseAnalyser`, or when its `name` is already taken by a built-in or by a plugin accepted earlier
in the same call; otherwise it appends the class. The warnings name the entry point.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: plugin_classes does not guard a plugin class with no name
STATEMENT: >>>
`plugin_classes()` raises `AttributeError` when a loaded `BaseAnalyser` subclass defines no `name` attribute,
and does not catch an exception raised by `entry_points()` itself; in both cases the exception leaves
`plugin_classes`, `analyser_classes`, `load_analysers` and `module_weights`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test loads a plugin class without a `name`. Review checks that `taken.add(cls.name)` is outside the `try`
and that `getattr(cls, "name", None)` returns `None` for such a class, which is not in `taken`. Reported as a
defect against HLR-ANL-005.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: load_analysers
STATEMENT: >>>
`load_analysers(metadata=None)` constructs one new instance of every class of `analyser_classes()`, sets its
`metadata` attribute to the argument and returns the instances in order. A class whose constructor raises any
`Exception` is left out and a warning naming it is logged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the order, the plugin instance and the metadata. No test makes a constructor raise; review checks
that branch.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: module_weights and the built-in weights
STATEMENT: >>>
`module_weights()` returns `{name: float(weight)}` for every class of `analyser_classes()` whose `weight` is
truthy and above 0. The class weights of this part are `GPSAnalyser` 15.0, `BatteryAnalyser` 15.0,
`MotorAnalyser` 5.0, `ParameterAnalyser` 5.0 and `PowerAnalyser` 0.0; with the oscillation, vibration and EKF
weights of 20.0 each the built-in total is 100.0. A plugin's weight is included as declared, with no rescaling.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-006

