No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads
`find_col` and `find_runs` in `helpers.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: run_seconds and sample_rate_hz
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_seconds(ts_us, start, end)` returns `(ts_us[end] - ts_us[start]) / 1e6` when `end` is inside the array;
otherwise `(ts_us[end - 1] - ts_us[start] + median sample interval) / 1e6` when the array has more than one
sample, else `0.0`. `sample_rate_hz(ts_us, default)` returns `1e6 / median sample interval`, or `default` when
there are fewer than 2 samples or the median interval is not above 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads
`run_seconds` and `sample_rate_hz` in `helpers.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: to_list and downsample
STATEMENT: >>>
`to_list(arr)` returns a list of floats with every NaN and infinite value replaced by `None`.
`downsample(ts_us, *series, n=500)` takes every `step`-th element, `step = max(1, ceil(len(ts_us) / n))`, of the
timestamps and of each series, and returns `[timestamps in ms, series 1, ...]` as `to_list` lists, so no list
is longer than `n` (`MAX_CHART_POINTS` = 500).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads
`to_list` and `downsample` in `helpers.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: when
STATEMENT: >>>
`when(start_us=None, end_us=None)` returns a dict with `timestamp_start_ms = int(start_us / 1e3)` and
`t_start_s = round(start_us / 1e6, 3)` when `start_us` is given and finite, and `timestamp_end_ms` and `t_end_s`
likewise for `end_us`; a missing or non-finite bound adds no key.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test names this requirement; the behaviour is exercised only indirectly by other tests. A review reads `when`
in `helpers.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: confidence
STATEMENT: >>>
`confidence(margin, duration_s=None, quality=1.0)` returns `round(m * d * q, 3)` with
`m = 0.5 + 0.5 * clamp(margin, 0, 1)`, `d = 1.0` when `duration_s` is `None` else
`0.4 + 0.6 * min(1, max(0, duration_s) / 2.0)`, and `q = clamp(quality, 0, 1)`. The result lies between 0.0 and
1.0; with full quality it is never below 0.2.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test asserts a confidence value. Review checks the three factors and the rounding against the function.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: clean
STATEMENT: >>>
`clean(obj)` returns a JSON-safe copy: dict keys become strings, lists, tuples and numpy arrays become lists,
numpy and Python booleans become `bool`, integers become `int`, floats become `float` with NaN and infinity
replaced by `None`, each applied recursively; any other object is returned unchanged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The modules of this part do not call `clean`; it is used by the report builder. No analyser test calls it
directly. Review checks each type branch and that `bool` is tested before `int`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-010

