[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Flight phases (flightmd_core/analysers/phases.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FlightPhases record
STATEMENT: >>>
`FlightPhases` holds `armed` and `in_air`, each a list of `(start_us, end_us)` windows, and `source`, one of
`"vehicle_status"`, `"vehicle_status+land_detected"` or `"whole_log"`. `known` is `False` only when `source` is
`"whole_log"`. `describe(phase)` returns `"whole log (no arming data)"` when not known, else `"in flight"` for
`"in_air"` and `"while armed"` for any other phase.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: Tests check `known`, `armed` and `in_air`. The `describe` strings are checked by review.
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: FlightPhases.mask
STATEMENT: >>>
`FlightPhases.mask(ts_us, phase="in_air")` returns a boolean array that is true where a timestamp lies inside
any window of the phase, both ends included; `"in_air"` selects the in-air windows and any other value the
armed windows. It returns all false when no timestamp falls in a window.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

