STATEMENT: >>>
`_first(topics, *names)` returns the first named topic that exists, has at least one row and has a `timestamp`
column, else `None`. `flight_phases` looks up `vehicle_status` then `vehicle_status_0`, and
`vehicle_land_detected` then `vehicle_land_detected_0`.
<<<
