RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Window intersection
STATEMENT: >>>
`_intersect(a, b)` returns, for every pair of one window from `a` and one from `b`, the overlap
`(max of starts, min of ends)` when the start is below the end.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: flight_phases: armed windows and the whole-log fallback
STATEMENT: >>>
`flight_phases(topics)` takes the rows of the status topic with both `timestamp` and `arming_state` present,
sorted by time, and builds the armed windows with `_windows` from `arming_state == 2` (`ARMED`). When there is
no status topic, no `arming_state` column or no armed window, it returns
`FlightPhases([(-inf, +inf)], [(-inf, +inf)], "whole_log")`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: flight_phases: in-air windows
STATEMENT: >>>
With armed windows, `flight_phases` returns `FlightPhases(armed, armed, "vehicle_status")` when there is no
land-detector topic or it has no `landed` column. Otherwise it builds the not-landed windows with `_windows`
from the rows with both `timestamp` and `landed` present, intersects them with the armed windows and returns
source `"vehicle_status+land_detected"`; when the intersection is empty the in-air windows are the armed
windows.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-007

