[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPS sample selection
STATEMENT: >>>
`GPSAnalyser.analyse` sorts the topic by `timestamp` and keeps the rows for which
`flight_phases(topics).mask(ts, "in_air")` is true. When the phases are not known and a `fix_type` column
exists, it also drops every row before the first row with `fix_type >= 3`; when no row has a 3D fix nothing is
dropped.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPS sample rate, sustain length and fix mask
STATEMENT: >>>
`GPSAnalyser.analyse` computes the rate of the kept rows with `sample_rate_hz(ts, 5.0)`, the sustain length
`sustain_n = max(1, round(SUSTAIN_S * rate))` samples with `SUSTAIN_S` = 2.0 s, and `has_fix` as
`fix_type >= 3` per row, or all true when there is no `fix_type` column.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.no_fix
STATEMENT: >>>
`GPSAnalyser._fix` returns no finding and penalty 0 when no kept sample has `fix_type < 3`. When every kept
sample has `fix_type < 3` it returns one CRITICAL finding of kind `gps.no_fix`, confidence 0.9, window from the
first to the last kept sample, and penalty 30.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.fix_lost
STATEMENT: >>>
When some but not all kept samples have `fix_type < 3`, `GPSAnalyser._fix` measures each run with
`run_seconds` and, when the longest is `FIX_LOSS_MIN_S` (1.0 s) or more, returns one CRITICAL finding of kind
`gps.fix_lost` with the worst fix label from `FIX_LABELS` in the title, the count of runs and the longest
duration in the text, the window of the longest run, confidence `confidence(longest / 1.0 - 1, longest)` and
penalty 30.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-034
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.fix_degraded
STATEMENT: >>>
When the longest run below 3D is shorter than 1.0 s, `GPSAnalyser._fix` returns one WARNING finding of kind
`gps.fix_degraded`, the window of the longest run, confidence `confidence(number of runs / 5.0, longest)` and
penalty 15.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-035
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.sat_drop
STATEMENT: >>>
When `satellites_used` exists, `GPSAnalyser.analyse` sets counts below 0 or above `SAT_MAX_VALID` (60) to NaN.
`_satellites` ignores samples without a 3D fix, takes for each sample the minimum over that sample and the next
`n - 1`, `n = max(2, round(SAT_DROP_WINDOW_S * rate))` with `SAT_DROP_WINDOW_S` = 5.0 s, and at the first sample
where the count exceeds that minimum by `SAT_DROP_THRESH` (4) or more returns one WARNING finding of kind
`gps.sat_drop`, window from that sample to the minimum, confidence `confidence(drop / 4 - 1)` and penalty 15.
Later drops add no finding.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-036
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.hdop
STATEMENT: >>>
`GPSAnalyser.analyse` reads the column `hdop`, or `eph` when there is no `hdop`, sets values at or below 0, at
or above `HDOP_UNKNOWN` (50.0) and samples without a 3D fix to NaN, and takes the rolling median over
`sustain_n` samples (windows holding a NaN give NaN). `_hdop` takes the highest rolling median: above
`HDOP_CRITICAL` (4.0) it returns a CRITICAL finding with penalty 30, above `HDOP_WARNING` (2.0) a WARNING with
penalty 15, both of kind `gps.hdop`, with the window of the run above 2.0 that holds the peak and confidence
`confidence(worst / threshold - 1, run duration)`. The same thresholds and the title text "HDOP" are used when
the column is `eph`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: Tests use the `hdop` column. The `eph` fallback is checked by review.
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-037
STATUS: Active
TITLE: gps.jamming
STATEMENT: >>>
`GPSAnalyser._jamming` takes the rolling median of `jamming_indicator` over `sustain_n` samples; a peak above
`JAMMING_CRITICAL` (180) sets level critical and above `JAMMING_WARNING` (100) level warning. It takes the
rolling minimum of `jamming_state` over `sustain_n` samples; a peak of `JAM_STATE_CRITICAL` (3) or more raises
the level to critical and of `JAM_STATE_WARNING` (2) or more to at least warning. With a level set it returns
one finding of kind `gps.jamming`: CRITICAL, confidence 0.85, penalty 30; or WARNING, confidence 0.6, penalty
15. The window spans the samples where the indicator median is above 100, else those where the state minimum is
2 or more.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-038
STATUS: Active
