- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Internal resistance and sag
STATEMENT: >>>
`BatteryAnalyser._sag` steps through the log in windows of `IR_WINDOW_S` (10.0 s) from the first timestamp. In
each window with at least `IR_MIN_SAMPLES` (10) samples and a current range of at least
`max(IR_MIN_STEP_A, 0.2 * (95th - 5th percentile of the current))`, `IR_MIN_STEP_A` = 2.0 A, it fits
`V = a + b * t - R * I` by least squares. It returns `(None, None)` when no window qualifies. Otherwise the pack
resistance is `max(0, median of R)` in ohm and the sag per cell is
`R * max(0, peak - resting) / n_cells` in V, where `peak` is the 99th percentile of the current and `resting`
the lowest 10-sample rolling median of the current.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-049
STATUS: Active
TITLE: battery.sag
STATEMENT: >>>
`BatteryAnalyser._sag_finding` returns one finding of kind `battery.sag` when the sag per cell is above
`SAG_CRITICAL_PER_CELL` (1.00 V; CRITICAL, penalty 30) or above `SAG_WARNING_PER_CELL` (0.50 V; WARNING, penalty
15), with confidence `confidence(sag / threshold - 1, quality=0.8 when the cell count is estimated else 1.0)`,
the time of the highest current sample as window start, and a text that says when the cell count was estimated
from voltage.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-050
STATUS: Active
TITLE: battery.c_rate
STATEMENT: >>>
Only when a rated capacity is known, `BatteryAnalyser._c_rate` takes the rolling median of the current over the
number of samples in 1 s (`round(1e6 / max(median sample interval in us, 1))`, at least 1), and divides its peak
by the capacity in Ah. Above `CRATE_WARNING` (30.0) it returns one WARNING finding of kind `battery.c_rate`,
confidence `confidence(c_rate / 30 - 1)`, window start at the peak, penalty 10. It always returns the C-rate.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: battery.capacity_fade
STATEMENT: >>>
Only when both a state of charge and a rated capacity are known, `BatteryAnalyser._capacity_fade` returns no
finding when: fewer than 10 state-of-charge samples are finite; or the state of charge is within
`CIRCULAR_TOLERANCE` (0.03) of `1 - drawn / capacity` at every finite sample; or the fall in state of charge
between the first and last finite sample is below `MIN_USED_FRACTION` (0.3); or
`estimated * CAPACITY_FADE_FACTOR (1.15) >= capacity`, with `estimated = charge drawn between those samples /
fall`. Otherwise it returns one WARNING finding of kind `battery.capacity_fade`, with no time window, confidence
`confidence(fade percent / 30.0, quality=min(1, fall / 0.6))` and penalty 15.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-016

