[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-072
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Firmware tables
STATEMENT: >>>
`load_tables()` reads every `*.json` file of `data/param_tables/` once per process, in name order, and adds to
each a `series` tuple, the first two integers of its `version`. Each file holds `autopilot` (`px4` or
`ardupilot`), `vehicle` (null, `copter`, `plane` or `rover`), `version`, `source`, `generated` and `params`, a
map from parameter name to any of `default`, `min`, `max`, `unit`, `type`, `reboot_required`, `read_only`. The
shipped files are PX4 1.13.3, 1.14.0 and 1.15.0 and ArduPilot Copter, Plane and Rover 4.6.3 and 4.7.1; the
ArduPilot tables hold no `default`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: Tests load the tables and use `series`, `vehicle`, `default`, `min`, `max`. The list of versions is checked by review of the file headers.
ALLOCATION: analysers, data
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-073
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Firmware series from the metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`firmware_series(metadata, autopilot)` returns `(major, minor)` from the first `<digits>.<digits>` found in
`metadata.px4_version` then `metadata.firmware_version` for `"px4"`, and in `metadata.firmware_version` only for
any other autopilot, taking the first field whose major is above 0. It returns `None` when `metadata` is `None`
or no field matches.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
