[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-075
STATUS: Active
TITLE: pick_table: nearest table
STATEMENT: >>>
`pick_table(autopilot, vehicle, series)` takes the tables of the autopilot (for ArduPilot with a known vehicle,
of that vehicle only) and returns `({}, "")` when there are none. With a series, and for ArduPilot a known
vehicle, it returns the `params` of the table with the lowest
`abs(major difference) * 100 + abs(minor difference)`, the higher minor winning a tie, and the text
`"<name> <major>.<minor> metadata"` with name `PX4` or `Ardu<Vehicle>`. There is no limit on the distance: any
older or newer version gets the nearest table.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-076
STATUS: Active
TITLE: pick_table: merged table
STATEMENT: >>>
With no series, or for ArduPilot with no known vehicle, `pick_table` merges the candidate tables in series
order: for each parameter the fields other than `min` and `max` are taken from the newest table that states
them, `min` is the lowest and `max` the highest among the tables that state one (a table that states no bound
does not remove the bound), and the text is `"<name> metadata, widest range across releases"` with name `PX4`,
`Ardu<Vehicle>` or `ArduPilot`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-077
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ParameterAnalyser declaration and set-up
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParameterAnalyser` has `name` `"parameters"`, `display_name` `"Parameter Analysis"`, no required topic,
`weight` 5.0 and `is_applicable` always `True`. `analyse` returns `_skip("No parameters found in log.")` for an
empty parameter set. It takes the vehicle from `vehicle_from_params`, uses autopilot `"px4"` when that is
`"unknown"`, keeps the parameters that are real numbers and finite, converted with `f32`, and takes the table
from `pick_table(autopilot, ap_vehicle(...), firmware_series(...))` and the recommended ranges of that
autopilot.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
