[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-078
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter loop, health score and key metrics
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParameterAnalyser.analyse` runs `_range_check` on every kept parameter except those the table marks
`read_only` and, on a PX4 fixed_wing or rover, those whose name starts with `MC_` or `MPC_`; then evaluates
each entry of `DANGEROUS_COMBOS` of the same autopilot, leaving out on a PX4 fixed_wing or rover the entries
that name an `MC_` or `MPC_` parameter. It subtracts 30.0 per CRITICAL and 15.0 per WARNING finding from 100.0
and returns `health_score = max(0.0, ...)` and `key_metrics` `param_count` (all parameters in the log) and
`anomaly_count` (number of findings), both as floats.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: Tests cover the fixed-wing exclusion, the score and the findings. The `read_only` exclusion and the key metrics are checked by review.
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-079
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Range check: which limit is reported
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParameterAnalyser._range_check` reports the first limit broken, in this order: below the table `min`, above
the table `max` (both "firmware"), below the recommended `min`, above the recommended `max` (both
"recommended"). A value equal to a limit is in range. It returns `None` when no limit is broken or the
parameter is in neither the table nor the recommended ranges.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-080
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Range check: severity
STATEMENT: >>>
`_range_check` takes `lo` as the higher of the firmware and recommended minimum and `hi` as the lower of the
two maxima. The finding is CRITICAL when `abs(value - broken limit) / scale > 0.5`, with `scale = hi - lo` when
both exist and `hi > lo`, else `max(abs(broken limit), 1.0)`; or when the value is negative and `lo` (0 when
there is none) is 0 or more. Otherwise it is WARNING.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-081
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Range check: suggested value
STATEMENT: >>>
`_range_check` suggests the table `default` when one exists and it is not below `lo` and not above `hi`;
otherwise `lo` when the value is below a limit and `hi` when it is above one. The suggestion is passed through
`f32`. It is therefore always inside the range of the table that was picked (nearest or merged) and the
recommended range; it is not checked against the range of the log's own firmware when that differs from the
table, and for ArduPilot (no defaults) it is always the limit itself.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-082
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Range check: finding content
STATEMENT: >>>
`_range_check` returns a finding of kind `params.below_range` or `params.above_range` with title
`"Parameter Below Safe Range: <name>"` or `"Parameter Above Safe Range: <name>"`, a text giving the value, the
limit, its unit (omitted for `norm` and `%/100`), the table description in brackets when the limit is the
firmware's and the `why` text when it is a recommended one, a recommendation
`"Set <name> to <suggested> (usable range <lo> to <hi>)."` with `" Takes effect after a reboot."` added when
the table marks `reboot_required`, confidence 0.9 for a firmware limit and 0.8 for a recommended one, and one
`ParamRecommendation` with the parameter name, current value, suggested value, unit, direction `increase` when
below and `decrease` when above, and the reason.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-083
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Combination table
STATEMENT: >>>
`DANGEROUS_COMBOS` holds eight entries. PX4: `MC_ROLLRATE_P > 0.3` and `MC_ROLLRATE_D < 0.001` (WARNING,
`params.rate_p_high_d_low`, fix `MC_ROLLRATE_D` increase); `MC_PITCHRATE_P > 0.3` and `MC_PITCHRATE_D < 0.001`
(WARNING, same kind, fix `MC_PITCHRATE_D` increase); `MPC_XY_P > 1.5` and `MPC_XY_VEL_P_ACC < 1.5` (WARNING,
`params.pos_loop_risk`, fix `MPC_XY_P` decrease); `BAT_LOW_THR < BAT_CRIT_THR` (CRITICAL,
`params.bat_thr_inverted`, fix `BAT_LOW_THR` increase); `COM_RC_LOSS_T < 0.5` (WARNING, `params.rc_loss_short`,
fix `COM_RC_LOSS_T` increase). ArduPilot, no fix: `BATT_LOW_VOLT > 0`, `BATT_CRT_VOLT > 0` and
`BATT_LOW_VOLT <= BATT_CRT_VOLT` (CRITICAL, `params.bat_thr_inverted`); the same with `BATT_LOW_MAH` and
`BATT_CRT_MAH` (CRITICAL, `params.bat_thr_inverted`); `ARMING_CHECK == 0` (WARNING,
`params.arming_checks_off`).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
