[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-086
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Combination fix
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParameterAnalyser._combo_fix` returns no change when the entry has no fix, the fix parameter has no current
value, or the picked table has no `default` for it. Otherwise the target is the table default, except for
`BAT_LOW_THR` where it is `max(default, BAT_CRIT_THR + 0.05)`; the target is passed through `f32` and returned
as one `ParamRecommendation` (name, current value, target, direction, the entry's title as reason, no unit)
unless it does not move the value in the entry's direction, in which case no change is returned. The target is
not compared with the table `min` or `max` or the recommended range.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the `BAT_LOW_THR` and `MC_ROLLRATE_D` fixes. That the target is not bounded is checked by review
and reported as a defect (see HLR-ANL-024).
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-ANL-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-ANL-087
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter result when no parameter is known to any table
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParameterAnalyser.analyse` returns a skipped result (not assessed) with the reason "None of the <n> parameters
is in the <AUTOPILOT> tables (<autopilot> autopilot)." when the parameter set is not empty but none of its
finite numeric names is in the picked table, the recommended ranges of that autopilot or a combination rule of
that autopilot (for example a set that is neither PX4 nor ArduPilot, which is checked against the PX4 tables).
The table description appears only in the text of findings that report a firmware limit.
<<<
